// HDRP uses Deferred by default, but you can switch per-camera:
//
// On the Camera component:
// Rendering Path: Deferred (default) or Forward Only
//
// Deferred is better for:
// - Many lights in the scene
// - Complex lighting scenarios
// - Opaque geometry-heavy scenes
//
// Forward Only is needed for:
// - MSAA anti-aliasing (Deferred can't do MSAA)
// - Custom shaders that don't write to G-buffers
// - Some VR applications
//
// HDRP also supports Forward+ (clustered forward) in newer versions,
// which combines benefits of both approaches.

// HDRP Project Setup:
// File → New Project → HDRP Template
